  "query_preview": ".. (Thursday through Friday)\n\nThe cold front is forecast to push south of the region by\nThursday, bringing notable relief as high temperatures drop into\nthe upper 70s and lower 80s. However, model guidance continues\nto diverge regarding the post-frontal air mass evolution. The\nGFS/GEFS suite drives the front cleanly south, ushering in a\ncooler, drier continental polar (cP) air mass through Saturday.\nConversely, the ECMWF/EPS models favor a quicker progression,\nlifting the front back northward across Illinois by Friday and\nreintroducing stifling humidity and thunderstorm chances. Given\nthe uncertainty, rain chances remain in the forecast through\nlate week due to the CWA's proximity to the stalled baroclinic\nzone.",
